- Ruling: Do not add or run pytest/unit tests during Tasks 1–5 because the user explicitly deferred them until the build is finished; use direct parity probes, real offline CLI reconciliation, compilation, and diff checks — if these checks miss a regression, formal test coverage must catch it only after the user ends the build phase.
- Ruling: Do not commit task changes because the current worktree already contains user-owned/uncommitted Task 11A/11B work and no commit/push/merge was authorized; task reviewers inspect the exact task files, implementer report, and path-scoped working-tree diff directly — the cost is that commit-range review packages cannot isolate edits automatically.
- Ruling: Treat CANSLIM as the feature basis/reference family, not the optimization objective; classify exact Task 11 thresholds as active fixed optimizer candidates and causal/data/execution integrity as invariants — if this interpretation is wrong, the later optimizer surface would need reclassification but no strategy behavior changes in this plan.

